------------------------------------------------------------------------
LiteIBP (T. Peraro): origin of the derivative routines
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The derivative routines of AMFlow's Kira interface are from LiteIBP.m by
Tiziano Peraro, part of FiniteFlow MathTools:

  https://github.com/peraro/finiteflow-mathtools  (packages/LiteIBP.m)

  T. Peraro, "FiniteFlow: multivariate functional reconstruction using
  finite fields and dataflow graphs", arXiv:1905.08019.

AMFlow states this in its source, ibp_interface/Kira/interface.m:
"compute derivatives (code from LiteIBP.m provided by T.Peraro)"
(line 280 at commit efda1db, version 1.2; line 400 at tag 2.0).

In this repository:

  - src/ibp/libp_deriv.cpp and include/amflow/ibp/libp_deriv.hpp are
    upstream AMFlow.cpp's C++ port of that block of AMFlow's Kira
    interface.
  - The BootLoops fork added to them the momentum-derivative chain rule
    for kinematic invariants defined through replacement rules.  It
    takes the place of LiteIBP's LIBPDerivivative (LiteIBP.m line 565 at
    commit f77e2b5; Kira/interface.m line 383 at commit efda1db, line
    503 at tag 2.0), which upstream AMFlow.cpp had not implemented.

The finiteflow-mathtools repository carries no license file, at commit
f77e2b5 (2026-01-21) or at any of its 19 commits, and LiteIBP.m states
no license terms.  The Anthropic copyright and the MIT grant on the
BootLoops modifications do not cover the portion of these two files that
derives from LiteIBP.

